      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofsmithsburg.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Platted in 1814, the town grew along migration routes, the railroad, and farming advances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofsmithsburg.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "On July 5, 1863, Confederate General James Stuart and Union General Kilpatrick exchanged artillery over Smithsburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithsburg%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A cannon ball from that 1863 duel remains lodged in a Water Street building wall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithsburg%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Founded in 1813, Smithsburg is known for rolling hills, agritourism, and historic mid‑century architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitsmithsburg.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Smithsburg sits just west of Camp David and near the former Fort Ritchie army base.",
